    "text": "To solve this problem, we need to determine the number of questions Frank answered correctly. Let's denote the number of correct answers by \\( x \\), the number of incorrect answers by \\( y \\), and the number of unanswered questions by \\( z \\).\n\nGiven the information:\n- The total number of questions is 100.\n- Frank answered 80 questions.\n- Each correct answer scores 5 points.\n- Each incorrect answer scores -2 points.\n- Each unanswered question scores 0 points.\n- Frank's total score is 232 points.\n\nWe can set up the following equations based on the given information:\n\n1. The total number of questions:\n\\[\nx + y + z = 100\n\\]\n\n2. The number of answered questions:\n\\[\nx + y = 80\n\\]\n\n3. The total score:\n\\[\n5x - 2y = 232\n\\]\n\nFirst, we solve for \\( z \\) using the second equation:\n\\[\nz = 100 - (x + y) = 100 - 80 = 20\n\\]\n\nNext, we substitute \\( y = 80 - x \\) into the third equation:\n\\[\n5x - 2(80 - x) = 232\n\\]\n\nSimplify and solve for \\( x \\):\n\\[\n5x - 160 + 2x = 232\n\\]\n\\[\n7x - 160 = 232\n\\]\n\\[\n7x = 492\n\\]\n\\[\nx = \\frac{492}{7}\n\\]\n\\[\nx = 70\n\\]\n\nThus, Frank answered \\(\\boxed{70}\\) questions correctly.",
